{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785106831,"nonce":"s43QK6fC12fnTd0ALoFYRhvN0O8=","message":"Closing as NOT REPRODUCIBLE — I checked the workflow and the premise does not hold.\n\nThe `paths:` filter this ticket describes sits under `pull_request:` only\n(`.github/workflows/image.yml:26-38`), and it already lists `crates/**` at :32 —\nso a change to the fetcher's source (a bin target of\n`crates/scarab-workspace-client`) does trigger the image job on a PR.\n\nMore decisively, the `push:` trigger at :23-25 is `branches: [main]` with **no\n`paths:` filter at all**, and there is no per-image gating inside the job — the\nonly `if:` conditions are the four `github.event_name != 'pull_request'`\npush/login guards at :89, :110, :117, :129. The matrix at :60 builds all four\nimages unconditionally, `scarab-wsfetch` included.\n\nSo merging to `main` rebuilds and republishes `scarab-wsfetch:edge` regardless of\nwhich files changed. `DEFAULT_WSFETCH_IMAGE` is not stale-by-construction.\n\nWorth recording the general lesson, since this is the second time it has bitten\nin this repo: check the trigger primitives before recording a blocker. A\n`paths:` filter under one trigger says nothing about the others.","files":null}]}